{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:f4cbfc58a683894a66b028420969bb75a35fe4acda1bd3dce0024062c11b2041", "sample_idx": 1, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "\"To access the print version of the article, a link is provided. The rules for the Sudoku puzzle are explained, with a notable exception regarding cells within grey lines. These cells have a unique requirement, where the numbers inside them must sum up to the figures indicated in the corner. This adds a layer of complexity to the traditional Sudoku rules. The goal is to fill in the numbers without repeating any within each shape formed by the grey lines.\"\n\n\n \nAddition to the traditional Sudoku rules, the numbers in the cells contained within grey lines must add up to the figures in the corner. This means that players need to think strategically about which numbers to place in each cell. The constraint of not repeating numbers within each shape formed by grey lines adds an extra level of challenge. The puzzle requires careful planning and attention to detail. The rules are designed to test the player's problem-solving skills.\n\n\n \nThe completed puzzle can be found in next week's Observer Digital Edition. This provides a solution for those who are struggling to solve it or want to check their answers. The publication offers a convenient way to access the completed puzzle, allowing readers to compare their work with the official solution. The Observer Digital Edition is a valuable resource for Sudoku enthusiasts. It provides a convenient and accessible way to enjoy the puzzle.\n\n\n \nThe rules of the Sudoku puzzle are designed to be fun and challenging. The unique twist of the cells within grey lines adding up to the figures in the corner requires players to think creatively. The puzzle is a great way to exercise the brain and improve problem-solving skills. The sense of accomplishment when completing the puzzle is rewarding. The challenge of the Sudoku puzzle is what makes it so engaging and entertaining.\n\n\n \nThe Sudoku puzzle is a popular activity for many people. The combination of logic and reasoning required to solve it makes it appealing to those who enjoy a challenge. The puzzle is a great way to relax and unwind, while also exercising the brain. The unique rules and constraints of the puzzle make it a fun and engaging activity. The Observer Digital Edition provides a convenient way to access the completed puzzle, making it a valuable resource for Sudoku enthusiasts.", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"To", "logprob": -0.530904233455658}, {"token": " access", "logprob": -0.1004420816898346}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.018160497769713402}, {"token": " print", "logprob": -0.00867396779358387}, {"token": " version", "logprob": -0.00012337400403339416}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.004078523721545935}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.008675622753798962}, {"token": " article", "logprob": -0.3157201409339905}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.004694037139415741}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.04559532180428505}, {"token": " link", "logprob": -0.02002721093595028}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.005243122112005949}, {"token": " provided", "logprob": -0.00020382710499688983}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.6577472686767578}, {"token": " The", "logprob": -0.00615546153858304}, {"token": " rules", "logprob": -0.13191324472427368}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.023945653811097145}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.15292957425117493}, {"token": " Sudoku", "logprob": -0.03891653195023537}, {"token": " puzzle", "logprob": -0.0010239601833745837}, {"token": " are", "logprob": -0.0009233264136128128}, {"token": " explained", "logprob": -0.6223216652870178}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -3.766942609217949e-05}, {"token": " with", "logprob": -0.04575180262327194}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.025936709716916084}, {"token": " notable", "logprob": -1.461712121963501}, {"token": " exception", "logprob": -0.00017712931730784476}, {"token": " 